\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n‖f(t)‖=\\sqrt{7}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186308554 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "92053541-63fa-5cca-b3d8-0f4864c31051" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Norm of a Vector With Respect to a Given Inner Product"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d972ed08-7aac-5a90-b5ab-eb8eb907ed35" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{22}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186308556} {:answer/id #uuid "da744d9b-ef30-53a5-bb4c-135bf8e5357e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{35}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186308557} {:answer/id #uuid "aa339327-5e52-5d2a-9032-1e4d16ee4128" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186308558} {:answer/id #uuid "b70c44a5-1bcd-5ca1-b38e-32ce49bc0605" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\sqrt{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186308559} {:answer/id #uuid "13fdf335-5977-5424-912e-dcba9a706e74" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186308560}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "da744d9b-ef30-53a5-bb4c-135bf8e5357e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{35}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186308557} :answer-field/id #uuid "92ecd833-0dff-512b-9685-3eab07ff25a6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186308555}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "5daddfb3-e7f8-5c06-afbf-1d755d1586e7" :question/math-academy-id "q-97413" :question/problem "An inner product on $V={R}^{3}$ is defined as $⟨x,y⟩=2{x}_{1}{y}_{1}+2{x}_{2}{y}_{2}+{x}_{3}{y}_{3}.$ \nCalculate the norm of the vector $v=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]$ under this inner product." :question/worked-solution "The norm of a vector $v$ with respect to an inner product $⟨\\cdot ,\\cdot ⟩$ is defined as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖v‖=\\sqrt{⟨v,v⟩}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComputing $‖v‖$ using our definition, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖v‖ & =\\sqrt{⟨v,v⟩} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{2\\cdot (3\\cdot 3)+2\\cdot (2\\cdot 2)+(-3)\\cdot (-3)} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{18+8+9} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{35}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186308561 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "92053541-63fa-5cca-b3d8-0f4864c31051" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Norm of a Vector With Respect to a Given Inner Product"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "47931536-0095-549d-a99b-74feacf602f8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\sqrt{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186308563} {:answer/id #uuid "eb6e8e7e-248f-59cf-8a59-08bbadaef26d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186308564} {:answer/id #uuid "4bf39b1b-07c3-5001-b262-237bbbd1f83d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186308565} {:answer/id #uuid "1b977c9a-ac18-58e1-83cb-4d6aaf3dc08f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186308566} {:answer/id #uuid "0c5b7d37-7358-53a5-80ae-de4a6572870e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186308567}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1b977c9a-ac18-58e1-83cb-4d6aaf3dc08f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186308566} :answer-field/id #uuid "7c4c3439-b2a7-5ded-a938-d736497518ba" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186308562}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "945b9281-03c5-5d25-8f73-c3f9ea58c409" :question/math-academy-id "q-97414" :question/problem "An inner product on $V={R}^{3}$ is defined as $⟨x,y⟩=2{x}_{1}{y}_{1}+3{x}_{2}{y}_{2}+2{x}_{3}{y}_{3}.$ \nCalculate the norm of the vector $v=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]$ under this inner product." :question/worked-solution "The norm of a vector $v$ with respect to an inner product $⟨\\cdot ,\\cdot ⟩$ is defined as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖v‖=\\sqrt{⟨v,v⟩}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComputing $‖v‖$ using our definition, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖v‖ & =\\sqrt{⟨v,v⟩} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{2\\cdot (1\\cdot 1)+3\\cdot ((-2)\\cdot (-2))+2\\cdot ((-1)\\cdot (-1))} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{2+12+2} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{16} \\\\  & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186308568 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "5e023193-7494-5e3a-bd6e-e15ae0e9a1bd" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Norm of a Vector in an Inner Product Space of Polynomials"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2ffde8f9-ecbe-50f1-99d4-3a8686ff4281" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186308570} {:answer/id #uuid "8bd201b4-faf6-5032-9249-1454a6d3162d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186308571} {:answer/id #uuid "5c7c0d23-c009-5c2a-92f9-d3ed2ce3e038" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186308572} {:answer/id #uuid "cc052681-1ae2-59db-85f9-9af44265211a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186308573} {:answer/id #uuid "0f1d2ff6-930f-5906-99eb-91e73481eb08" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186308574}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5c7c0d23-c009-5c2a-92f9-d3ed2ce3e038" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186308572} :answer-field/id #uuid "b9826e7c-0174-5202-93b2-53300ad5735a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186308569}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "4e07ea74-65b4-594e-914e-fe1b3c0f9704" :question/math-academy-id "q-97418" :question/problem "Let $V={R}_{2}[t]$ be the vector space of all polynomials of degree at most $2,$ equipped with the inner product\n\n$$\n⟨x(t),y(t)⟩=x(0)y(0)+x(1)y(1)+x(2)y(2).\n$$\n\nCalculate the norm of the vector $p(t)=2+t-{t}^{2}.$" :question/worked-solution "The norm of a vector $p(t)$ with respect to an inner product $⟨\\cdot ,\\cdot ⟩$ is defined as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖p(t)‖=\\sqrt{⟨p(t),p(t)⟩}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $p(t)=2+t-{t}^{2},$ we obtain\n\n$$\np(0)=2,\\,p(1)=2,\\,p(2)=0.\n$$\n\nComputing $‖p(t)‖$ using our definition, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖p(t)‖ & =\\sqrt{⟨p(t),p(t)⟩} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{p(0)p(0)+p(1)p(1)+p(2)p(2)} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{[p(0)]^{2}+[p(1)]^{2}+[p(2)]^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(2)^{2}+(2)^{2}+(0)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{4+4+0} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{8} \\\\  & =2\\sqrt{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186134475 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "5e023193-7494-5e3a-bd6e-e15ae0e9a1bd" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Norm of a Vector in an Inner Product Space of Polynomials"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "fcb93c50-b6a4-5ed0-ba6e-c1f5258956ee" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4\\sqrt{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186133293} {:answer/id #uuid "04fdfe8a-728b-5d28-bf40-3c2920036919" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186133294} {:answer/id #uuid "47425b26-9946-5769-922a-472f69b0c2c7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5\\sqrt{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186133295} {:answer/id #uuid "6e83664f-4798-5180-93bd-0aa51180ebdf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186133296} {:answer/id #uuid "710e8117-3952-528b-865e-9de244ca3297" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4\\sqrt{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186133297}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "04fdfe8a-728b-5d28-bf40-3c2920036919" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186133294} :answer-field/id #uuid "b8bf7216-e5ce-5571-8b5d-92a21be1635d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186133292}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "17b9d976-83b8-5275-b6d4-e009224e5ca4" :question/math-academy-id "q-97420" :question/problem "Let $V={R}_{2}[t]$ be the vector space of all polynomials of degree at most $2,$ equipped with the inner product\n\n$$\n⟨x(t),y(t)⟩=x(0)y(0)+x(2)y(2)+x(3)y(3).\n$$\n\nCalculate the norm of the vector $p(t)=4-2t+{t}^{2}.$" :question/worked-solution "The norm of a vector $p(t)$ with respect to an inner product $⟨\\cdot ,\\cdot ⟩$ is defined as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖p(t)‖=\\sqrt{⟨p(t),p(t)⟩}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $p(t)=4-2t+{t}^{2},$ we obtain\n\n$$\np(0)=4,\\,p(2)=4,\\,p(3)=7.\n$$\n\nComputing $‖p(t)‖$ using our definition, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖p(t)‖ & =\\sqrt{⟨p(t),p(t)⟩} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{p(0)p(0)+p(2)p(2)+p(3)p(3)} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{[p(0)]^{2}+[p(2)]^{2}+[p(3)]^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(4)^{2}+(4)^{2}+(7)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{16+16+49} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{81} \\\\  & =9.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186308575 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "5e023193-7494-5e3a-bd6e-e15ae0e9a1bd" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Norm of a Vector in an Inner Product Space of Polynomials"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1fbacd75-9738-56dc-b6b5-921fcb119720" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4\\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186308577} {:answer/id #uuid "fc2bdcea-f2f0-5a18-8b5a-3279b03a9b8e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{10}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186308578} {:answer/id #uuid "aefb5a38-b4d0-556c-a547-8ad1308074f8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{34}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186308579} {:answer/id #uuid "2b437129-9914-52c7-aee1-27516a9012f0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186308580} {:answer/id #uuid "6ff35215-6916-5a16-940d-5a2bcbd67ed2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186308581}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "aefb5a38-b4d0-556c-a547-8ad1308074f8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{34}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186308579} :answer-field/id #uuid "be1ea524-178e-573e-a3fc-1d252368aebb" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186308576}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "294160f3-8768-53a9-8a25-c924f493cc11" :question/math-academy-id "q-97422" :question/problem "Let $V={R}_{2}[t]$ be the vector space of all polynomials of degree at most $2,$ equipped with the inner product\n\n$$\n⟨x(t),y(t)⟩=x(1)y(1)+x(0)y(0)+x(-1)y(-1).\n$$\n\nCalculate the norm of the vector $p(t)=4-{t}^{2}.$" :question/worked-solution "The norm of a vector $p(t)$ with respect to an inner product $⟨\\cdot ,\\cdot ⟩$ is defined as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖p(t)‖=\\sqrt{⟨p(t),p(t)⟩}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $p(t)=4-{t}^{2},$ we obtain\n\n$$\np(1)=3,\\,p(0)=4,\\,p(-1)=3.\n$$\n\nComputing $‖p(t)‖$ using our definition, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖p(t)‖ & =\\sqrt{⟨p(t),p(t)⟩} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{p(1)p(1)+p(0)p(0)+p(-1)p(-1)} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{[p(1)]^{2}+[p(0)]^{2}+[p(-1)]^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(3)^{2}+(4)^{2}+(3)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{9+16+9} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{34}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186308582 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "5e023193-7494-5e3a-bd6e-e15ae0e9a1bd" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Norm of a Vector in an Inner Product Space of Polynomials"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0cc5c60d-9e70-5d4e-9225-20400855a68a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{42}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186308584} {:answer/id #uuid "d43bde1b-fa03-5c0a-aa29-f4f6493c0650" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186308585} {:answer/id #uuid "c34d5bb2-ad98-5ec6-9662-b23415bb77e1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\sqrt{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186308586} {:answer/id #uuid "39069c42-1238-5182-a60d-a057d0829972" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186308587} {:answer/id #uuid "1d6e4c7e-42c8-567e-902f-8ef06e680fd2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\sqrt{11}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186308588}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0cc5c60d-9e70-5d4e-9225-20400855a68a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{42}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186308584} :answer-field/id #uuid "4a34ca04-ed6c-5c04-ad43-438ffc89c787" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186308583}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "7690c503-491a-5df3-8fbf-bbfb20b8c977" :question/math-academy-id "q-97425" :question/problem "Let $V={R}_{2}[t]$ be the vector space of all polynomials of degree at most $2,$ equipped with the inner product\n\n$$\n⟨x(t),y(t)⟩=x(0)y(0)+x(2)y(2)+x(3)y(3).\n$$\n\nCalculate the norm of the vector $p(t)=5-3t.$" :question/worked-solution "The norm of a vector $p(t)$ with respect to an inner product $⟨\\cdot ,\\cdot ⟩$ is defined as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖p(t)‖=\\sqrt{⟨p(t),p(t)⟩}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $p(t)=5-3t,$ we obtain\n\n$$\np(0)=5,\\,p(2)=-1,\\,p(3)=-4.\n$$\n\nComputing $‖p(t)‖$ using our definition, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖p(t)‖ & =\\sqrt{⟨p(t),p(t)⟩} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{p(0)p(0)+p(2)p(2)+p(3)p(3)} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{[p(0)]^{2}+[p(2)]^{2}+[p(3)]^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(5)^{2}+(-1)^{2}+(-4)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{25+1+16} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{42}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186308589 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "090d6747-55e2-548b-84f2-88f6c732518f" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Norm of a Vector in an Inner Product Space of Continuous Functions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "01bc5cd8-5240-5e22-9ec2-bbe3e86b6cef" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{3\\pi +5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186308591} {:answer/id #uuid "a7cf3cb0-2652-5d0b-8b77-07ad50054bdf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\sqrt{\\pi }" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186308592} {:answer/id #uuid "7894d503-d09b-5371-906d-8e31e371fd4b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{\\pi }" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186308593} {:answer/id #uuid "acb04503-aa91-5c5c-9735-d52639e75e88" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{3\\pi }" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186308594} {:answer/id #uuid "1f595139-028b-5947-9d8e-761553179efe" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{9\\pi +5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186308595}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "acb04503-aa91-5c5c-9735-d52639e75e88" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{3\\pi }" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186308594} :answer-field/id #uuid "d2dd4f47-8756-5819-a060-18b416d2a767" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186308590}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "5583d7b5-f24f-5ebd-b60e-17939249b38f" :question/math-academy-id "q-97712" :question/problem "Let $V=C[\\pi ,2\\pi ]$ be the vector space of all functions that are continuous on $[\\pi ,2\\pi ],$ equipped with the inner product \n\n$$\n⟨x(t),y(t)⟩={\\int }_{\\pi }^{2\\pi }x(t)y(t)\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nCalculate the norm of the vector $f(t)=2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+1.$" :question/worked-solution "The norm of a vector $f(t)$ with respect to an inner product $⟨\\cdot ,\\cdot ⟩$ is defined as\n\n$$\n‖f(t)‖=\\sqrt{⟨f(t),f(t)⟩}.\n$$\n\nComputing the inner product using our definition, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨f(t),f(t)⟩ & ={\\int }_{\\pi }^{2\\pi }(f(t))^{2}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\pi }^{2\\pi }\\,(2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+1)^{2}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\pi }^{2\\pi }\\,(4{cos}^{2}⁡t+4\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+1)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\pi }^{2\\pi }((2+2\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t)+4\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+1)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\pi }^{2\\pi }(3+2\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t+4\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =(3t+\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t+4\\operatorname{sin}⁡t){|}_{\\pi }^{2\\pi } \\\\  & =(6\\pi +0+0)-(3\\pi +0+0) \\\\  & =3\\pi .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that we made use of the trigonometric identity \n\n$$\n{cos}^{2}⁡t=\\frac{1+\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t}{2}.\n$$\n\nFinally then,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖f(t)‖ & =\\sqrt{3\\pi }.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186308596 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "466fb505-1ff3-5b27-a5f7-0ea5b31b2927" :knowledge-point/title "Normalizing a Vector in an Inner Product Space"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a42e1b67-0009-55bc-8150-c3e441a30aa9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{10}}{10}(2-3t)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186308598} {:answer/id #uuid "3e432c84-b564-5ea2-9ef1-8ccfe3209b99" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2-3t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186308599} {:answer/id #uuid "366aae35-1927-5ea2-b1da-cc1e8e766e38" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{13}}{13}(3t-2)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186308600} {:answer/id #uuid "8aa81a03-683d-5b3c-919b-d9e0d3beb28f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{13}}{13}(2-3t)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186308601} {:answer/id #uuid "2a79ae09-2af0-5a45-b73f-df971c273f63" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}(2-3t)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186308602}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3e432c84-b564-5ea2-9ef1-8ccfe3209b99" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2-3t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186308599} :answer-field/id #uuid "8c90574b-107a-5d1f-ace1-e8e7f2db2ffe" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186308597}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "4c4fa733-f9a5-51a2-9ccc-317ee77679df" :question/math-academy-id "q-97721" :question/problem "Let $V=C[0,1]$ be the vector space of all functions that are continuous on $[0,1],$ equipped with the inner product \n\n$$\n⟨x(t),y(t)⟩={\\int }_{0}^{1}x(t)y(t)\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nNormalize the vector $f(t)=2-3t.$" :question/worked-solution "The norm of a vector $f(t)$ with respect to an inner product $⟨\\cdot ,\\cdot ⟩$ is defined as\n\n$$\n‖f(t)‖=\\sqrt{⟨f(t),f(t)⟩}.\n$$\n\nComputing the inner product using our definition, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨f(t),f(t)⟩ & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{(2-3t)}^{2}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}\\,(4-12t+9{t}^{2})\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={(4t-6{t}^{2}+3{t}^{3})|}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =4-6+3 \\\\  & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n‖f(t)‖=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1}}=1.\n$$\n\nTo normalize the vector $f(t),$ we divide $f(t)$ by its norm $‖f(t)‖:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u(t) & =\\frac{f(t)}{‖f(t)‖} \\\\  & =\\frac{2-3t}{1} \\\\  & =2-3t\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186308603 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "466fb505-1ff3-5b27-a5f7-0ea5b31b2927" :knowledge-point/title "Normalizing a Vector in an Inner Product Space"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4e830c27-e5cb-5916-8f67-c7aef0e53df8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186308605} {:answer/id #uuid "7a4b9b81-5a16-5bb5-9d00-e657245d3072" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{6}}{6}[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186308606} {:answer/id #uuid "c5a0765c-c75c-53a4-8107-43ded4173630" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{11}}{11}[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186308607} {:answer/id #uuid "46dbf34c-4240-5507-808e-b3b6c54cb1a9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{4}[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186308608} {:answer/id #uuid "a38e81e7-84e3-53b7-925e-3eb09ea6ad9c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186308609}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4e830c27-e5cb-5916-8f67-c7aef0e53df8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186308605} :answer-field/id #uuid "6387a3c0-8fd8-5255-a956-ebb777c4aa46" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186308604}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "d095eb6a-2ae3-5699-bca7-a936ad3d6b9e" :question/math-academy-id "q-97725" :question/problem "An inner product on $V={R}^{3}$ is defined as $⟨x,y⟩=3{x}_{1}{y}_{1}+{x}_{2}{y}_{2}+3{x}_{3}{y}_{3}.$ \n\nNormalize the  vector $v=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]$ under this inner product." :question/worked-solution "The norm of a vector $v$ with respect to an inner product $⟨\\cdot ,\\cdot ⟩$ is defined as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖v‖=\\sqrt{⟨v,v⟩}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComputing the inner product using our definition, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨v,v⟩ & =3\\cdot (2\\cdot 2)+(-1)\\cdot (-1)+3\\cdot (1\\cdot 1) \\\\  & =12+1+3 \\\\  & =16.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖v‖ & =\\sqrt{16}=4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo normalize the vector $v$, we divide $v$ by its norm $‖v‖:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u & =\\frac{v}{‖v‖} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186308610 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "466fb505-1ff3-5b27-a5f7-0ea5b31b2927" :knowledge-point/title "Normalizing a Vector in an Inner Product Space"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7de7c998-a09f-5750-a9b5-aa4dc8b1ccf0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186308612} {:answer/id #uuid "cb20cb48-9c1d-55d1-8a85-5b808463d433" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{7}}{7}[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186308613} {:answer/id #uuid "b860d49b-45b1-56a0-b923-5dac24c33f3d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{35}}{35}[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186308614} {:answer/id #uuid "9d9ebcc3-4857-583e-b281-074cb0eb6d6b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{22}}{22}[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186308615} {:answer/id #uuid "b15945df-fbbb-5ef3-b4de-9e50b2425110" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{22}[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186308616}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b860d49b-45b1-56a0-b923-5dac24c33f3d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{35}}{35}[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186308614} :answer-field/id #uuid "b121e9c3-f2c7-5ee2-bf76-6405555aff01" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186308611}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "5fae5da3-e57f-5671-91de-202da267e1a4" :question/math-academy-id "q-97726" :question/problem "An inner product on $V={R}^{3}$ is defined as $⟨x,y⟩=2{x}_{1}{y}_{1}+2{x}_{2}{y}_{2}+{x}_{3}{y}_{3}.$ \n\nNormalize the  vector $v=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]$ under this inner product." :question/worked-solution "The norm of a vector $v$ with respect to an inner product $⟨\\cdot ,\\cdot ⟩$ is defined as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖v‖=\\sqrt{⟨v,v⟩}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComputing the inner product using our definition, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨v,v⟩ & =2\\cdot (3\\cdot 3)+2\\cdot (2\\cdot 2)+(-3)\\cdot (-3) \\\\  & =18+8+9 \\\\  & =35.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖v‖ & =\\sqrt{35}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo normalize the vector $v$, we divide $v$ by its norm $‖v‖:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u & =\\frac{v}{‖v‖} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{35}}[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{35}}{35}[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
